<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jonathan Trumbull</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1710">1710</a>–<a href="/years/1785">1785</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Jonathan Trumbull Sr.</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jonathan Trumbull was governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/connecticut">Connecticut</a> Colony from 1769 to 1784 and the only colonial governor to support the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolution">American Revolution</a>. Under him Connecticut kept its charter government and supplied the Continental Army with food, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and munitions, earning the name 'Provisions State'. He continued as governor of the new state until 1784.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jonathan-trumbull.jpg" alt="Jonathan Trumbull" width="250" height="311" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: After John Trumbull · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:JohnTrumbull.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
